al-flow and recy...&#10;justification: The candidate’s core abstraction is that&#10;material identification improves when chemometric spectral&#10;information is combined with visual appearance information.&#10;This maps directly onto the problem’s bottleneck of&#10;recognizing dirty, aged, pigmented, contaminated, multilayer,&#10;and...&#10;abstract: Identifying the material composition of objects is&#10;crucial for many recycling sector applications. Traditionally,&#10;object classification relies either on hyperspectral imaging&#10;(HSI), which analyses the chemometric properties of objects to&#10;infer material types, or on RGB imaging...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 5&#10;domain: industrial_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Sensor-based Sorting as a Key Enabler for Efficient&#10;Recycling and Recovery of Secondary Raw Materials—Insights&#10;from Case Studies&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Sensor-based sorting as a quality-gate&#10;for secondary raw materials', 'Case-study-derived linkage&#10;between sorting performance and recycling/recovery&#10;efficiency', 'Consistency and purity requirements for&#10;circular-economy usability', 'Technical-economic trade-off&#10;framing for sorting decisions']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate’s sorting-as-enabler&#10;framework by converting uncertainty-aware NIR/MIR material-&#10;state predictions into expected purity, recovery yield, and&#10;economic value metrics, then using those metrics to route&#10;contaminated, aged, multilayer, or #3–#7 plastics into acce...&#10;justification: The candidate paper provides a transferable&#10;organizing principle: sensor-based sorting should be evaluated&#10;not only by classification accuracy but by its ability to&#10;produce economically usable secondary material streams with&#10;sufficient quality and consistency. This maps direct...&#10;abstract: Abstract Secondary raw materials are a key&#10;prerequisite for a functioning circular economy; however,&#10;their use is limited by technical, economic, and regulatory&#10;challenges. From a technical perspective, it is crucial that&#10;secondary raw materials exhibit sufficiently high and c...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 6&#10;domain: industrial_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: &lt;i&gt;Quo vadis&lt;/i&gt; MFA? Integrated material flow analysis&#10;to support material efficiency&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Integrated material flow analysis (MFA)&#10;as a system-level organizing framework', 'Mass-balance and&#10;flow-accounting structures linking item-level material states&#10;to aggregate material streams', 'Material-efficiency and&#10;circular-economy decision support through flow-based scenario&#10;evaluation']&#10;combination_plan: Use integrated MFA as the backbone for&#10;translating item-level spectroscopic/sensor classifications&#10;and uncertainty estimates into material-flow models,&#10;recycling-yield predictions, and circular-economy decision&#10;metrics. The MFA structure can constrain and aggregate&#10;uncertain p...&#10;justification: The candidate paper’s focus on integrated&#10;material flow analysis maps directly onto the problem’s&#10;bottleneck of connecting item-level material-state recognition&#10;with material-flow analysis, recycling yield, and circular-&#10;economy decisions.&#10;abstract:" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f9cb9c;strokeColor=#b45f06;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="7386" width="620" height="3462" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step7_analogy_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step7" target="step7_analogy_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step8" value="Step 8 Inspiration Selection&#10;status: completed&#10;selected_count: 3&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeCol