ass-balance and&#10;flow-accounting structures linking item-level material states&#10;to aggregate material streams', 'Material-efficiency and&#10;circular-economy decision support through flow-based scenario&#10;evaluation']&#10;combination_plan: Use integrated MFA as the backbone for&#10;translating item-level spectroscopic/sensor classifications&#10;and uncertainty estimates into material-flow models,&#10;recycling-yield predictions, and circular-economy decision&#10;metrics. The MFA structure can constrain and aggregate&#10;uncertain p...&#10;justification: The candidate paper’s focus on integrated&#10;material flow analysis maps directly onto the problem’s&#10;bottleneck of connecting item-level material-state recognition&#10;with material-flow analysis, recycling yield, and circular-&#10;economy decisions.&#10;abstract:&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 1&#10;domain: same_field&#10;radius: R1&#10;title: An Innovative Route to Circular Rigid Plastics&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Logarithmic or hierarchical pairwise&#10;sorting to achieve many-class discrimination with modest&#10;separation capacity', 'Sensor fusion using color plus high-&#10;resolution NIR for grade-level plastic differentiation',&#10;'Mapping spectral signatures to downstream physical material&#10;properties such as melt flow viscosity and tensile strength',&#10;'Deep sorting as an organizing principle for linking item-&#10;level recognition to high-grade recycling and circular-economy&#10;outcomes']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the logarithmic sorting idea into an&#10;uncertainty-aware hierarchical routing/classification system&#10;for dirty, aged, pigmented, multilayer, and #3–#7 plastics,&#10;where cheap sensor fusion (color, NIR/MIR, and other available&#10;modalities) makes pairwise material-state distinct...&#10;justification: Although the candidate focuses on cleaner rigid&#10;flakes, its core abstraction—economically scalable deep&#10;sorting through pairwise differentiability, hierarchical&#10;decision routing, and spectral-to-property mapping—maps&#10;directly onto the problem’s need for robust, uncertainty-&#10;awa...&#10;abstract: An innovative route for plastics recycling is&#10;proposed, based on a combination of a logarithmic sorting&#10;process and colour plus high-resolution near-infrared (NIR)&#10;sensors. Although counterintuitive, it is shown that such a&#10;technology could sort clean flakes from rigid packagi..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#ead1dc;strokeColor=#a64d79;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="10948" width="620" height="1644" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step8_selected_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step8_selected_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step9" value="Step 9 Idea Generation&#10;status: completed&#10;idea_count: 1&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="12692" width="220" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step8_step_step9" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step_step9"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step9_ideas_panel" value="Step 9 Idea Generation + Novelty Check&#10;count: 1&#10;&#10;1. Presentation-Controlled Differentiable Mass-Balance Inference&#10;for Plastic Waste Sorting and Material-Flow Accounting&#10;novelty_level: medium&#10;motivation: Better plastic-waste management requires reliable&#10;stream-level data and sorting decisions that remain valid for&#10;dirty, aged, contaminated, pigmented, multilayer, and #3-#7&#10;plastics. Spectroscopic machine learning can characterize mixed&#10;plastic waste [Author et al.,&#10;2022](https://openalex.org/W4309475252), NIR hyperspectral&#10;cascade detection can identify contaminants in post-consumer&#10;packaging [Author et al., 2021]...&#10;methods: 1. Presentation-conditioned spectral unmixing: The&#10;observation model treats each conveyor view as a mixed scene&#10;rather than a clean isolated item, adapting remote-sensing&#10;unmixing and uncertainty-aware retrieval to plastic waste&#10;[Author et al., 2012](https://openalex.org/W2265885259). It&#10;ingests NIR, MIR, RGB, or false-color band ratios and explicitly&#10;conditions the likelihood on presentation variables such as&#10;singulation, overlap, layer thickness, belt speed, orientation,&#10;and view geometry. This extends prior s...&#10;novelty_justification: Relative to the provided references, the&#10;closest existing combination is the pairing of AI-enabled&#10;sorting for complex plastic waste streams with online mixed-&#10;plastic spectroscopic characterization and NIR hyperspectral&#10;contaminant detection. Those works overlap the proposed idea in&#10;problem setting, sensing modality, dirty or contaminated plastic&#10;streams, and industrial sorting relevance. However, they largely&#10;sto...&#10;improvement_suggestions: ['Derive formal identifiability or&#10;observability bounds for bulk mass composition as an explicit&#10;function of occlusion, layer thickness, item-mass priors, sensor&#10;noise, and available spectral channels, then show that the&#10;active presentation controller provably reduces those bounds&#10;under cost or throughput constraints.', 'Introduce a distinct&#10;mass-conserving inference primitive, such as constrained optimal&#10;transport, a differentiable conservation layer, or mass-balanced&#10;probabilistic assignment, that resolves ambiguous overlapping&#10;observations into stream mass rather than applying material-flow&#10;accounting only after classification.', 'Formulate presentation&#10